#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_sin_coefficient

#% text
# `fourier_sin_coefficient(f, t, n)` gives the `n`-th coefficient of the Fourier sine series of `f`, `2/pi` times the integral of `f sin(n t)` for `t` from 0 to `pi`: the sine coefficient of the odd extension of `f` from `[0, pi]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# With `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` the coefficient is `2 abs(b)/pi` times the integral of `f sin(b n t)` over `[0, pi/abs(b)]`.

#% item
# A symbolic `n` is taken to be a positive integer: the result is the generic coefficient, with the exceptional positive indices as cases of a `piecewise` (or a `discrete_delta`).

#% item
# Lists of variables and indices give the coefficients of the products of sines.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_sin_coefficient(t, t, n)
#% output
#= -2*(-1)^n/n

#% cell
fourier_sin_coefficient(t^3, t, 2)
#% output
#= 3/2 - pi^2

